Package: soilSIM
Title: Multi-Source Soil Property Simulation and Bayesian Data Fusion
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jonathan", "Maynard", email = "jjmaynard9@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A data-source-agnostic framework for simulating soil properties
    and fusing estimates from multiple soil data products. Provides
    percentile-triplet and arbitrary-percentile distribution fitting,
    correlated Monte Carlo simulation (including compositional texture
    handling via isometric log-ratio transforms), Gaussian-process depth-trend
    modeling, descriptive statistics/correlation analysis, and Bayesian
    updating/fusion in both scalar and raster-native forms. Ships with
    SSURGO and SOLUS100 data-source adapters (tabular acquisition/processing/
    infilling for SSURGO, raster fetch for SOLUS100) wired into the fusion
    pipeline as prior and likelihood sources respectively; the simulation and
    fusion core is designed to accommodate additional gridded soil data
    sources as further adapters.
